# Allen Relation: EQUALS
#
# EQUALS: A and B begin and end at exactly the same time.
#   A equals B  iff  A.start = B.start and A.end = B.end
#
# For point-in-time events (instantaneous), A.start = A.end and B.start = B.end,
# so EQUALS reduces to: event_a_date = event_b_date.
#
# Legal patterns that trigger EQUALS:
#   two legal acts occurring on the same date (signing + declaration)
#   "simultaneously", "on the same date as", "as of the same date"
#   a regulation and its implementing decree entering force together
#   "the amendment takes effect on the same date as the original"
#   multiple instruments signed at the same ceremony
#
# Grounded example (en_contracts_seed4):
#   Signing of Second ACP-EEC Convention [1979-10-31, 1979-10-31]
#   EQUALS declaration of understanding [1979-10-31, 1979-10-31].
#   Both are instantaneous events on 31 October 1979.

```catala
declaration scope AllenEquals:
  input interval_a_start content date   # start of the first period
  input interval_a_end content date     # end of the first period
  input interval_b_start content date   # start of the second period
  input interval_b_end content date     # end of the second period
  output is_equals content boolean      # both periods share start and end
```

## EQUALS

Both intervals share the same start and end dates.
For instantaneous events, set start = end for both.

```catala
scope AllenEquals:
  date round down
  definition is_equals equals
    (interval_a_start = interval_b_start) and
    (interval_a_end = interval_b_end)
```
